.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "YEELELO OS Assignment" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words and characters in a file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.br
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The wordCount() function reads a file and counts the number
of lines, words and characters in the file.

The results are stored in the variables pointed to by
lines, words and chars.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 on success and -1 if the file is NULL.

